{"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "query": "Unit tests for an Arduino Uno module: Kitchen timer with 8x2 LCD, two buttons, buzzer, battery gauge and EEPROM. Pins: pin 3 INPUT BUTTON1 start, HIGH = pressed (not connected in the test setup: reads LOW); pin 2 INPUT BUTTON2 +1 minute, HIGH = pressed (not connected in the test setup: reads LOW); pin 5 OUTPUT buzzer (tone); pin 14 INPUT battery voltage A0 (not connected: reads 0); pin 7 OUTPUT LCD 8x2 RS (E 8, DB4..DB7 = 9..12). Arduino API used: analogRead, delay, digitalRead, noTone, pinMode, sizeof, tone. Libraries: LiquidCrystal. Library API used: begin, clear, createChar, setCursor, write. Simulated devices: none. Functions to test: void ktimer_set_delay_scale(uint8_t percent), void ktimer_init(), void ktimer_loop(), void ktimer_loop_with(boolean button1, boolean button2), void count_down(void), void display_alarm_time(void), void alarm(void), void increase_alarm_time(void), boolean button_press(uint8_t pin), int battery_voltage(void), void display_battery(void), const char* ktimer_lcd_line(uint8_t row).", "embedding": [-0.047943115234375, 0.0023555755615234375, -0.02899169921875, -0.04248046875, -0.0219268798828125, 0.0161895751953125, 0.0246124267578125, -0.011383056640625, 0.02569580078125, 0.006683349609375, 0.0008616447448730469, -0.0374755859375, -0.020751953125, 0.0305938720703125, 0.041717529296875, 0.0120697021484375, -0.0011510848999023438, 0.01690673828125, -0.019317626953125, 0.039337158203125, 0.028228759765625, -0.014984130859375, 0.048553466796875, 0.0241241455078125, 0.0239105224609375, -0.07916259765625, 0.015777587890625, 0.0095977783203125, 0.00711822509765625, -0.0267333984375, 0.01247406005859375, -0.0213623046875, -0.0261993408203125, 1.7881393432617188e-05, -0.01373291015625, 0.02227783203125, 0.032073974609375, 0.01395416259765625, -0.0272064208984375, -0.055419921875, -0.05804443359375, -0.051361083984375, -0.0167083740234375, -0.02777099609375, -0.04852294921875, -0.0004668235778808594, -0